This extension demonstrates how to register tools dynamically at runtime using the `session_start` lifecycle event.

## Usage

```bash
# Load the extension
pi --extension examples/extensions/dynamic-tools.ts
```

## How It Works

This extension registers a custom tool called `dynamic_tool` that becomes available after the session starts. This is useful for:

- Tools that need to be initialized after the session is created
- Tools that depend on runtime state
- Tools that should only be available in certain contexts

## Example

```typescript
import { Type } from "@sinclair/typebox";

export default function (pi: ExtensionAPI) {
  // Register a tool that will be available after session_start
  pi.on("session_start", async () => {
    pi.registerTool({
      name: "dynamic_tool",
      label: "Dynamic Tool",
      description: "A tool registered at runtime",
      parameters: Type.Object({
        message: Type.String({ description: "Message to echo" }),
      }),
      async execute(toolCallId, params, onUpdate, ctx, signal) {
        return {
          content: [{ type: "text", text: `Dynamic tool received: ${params.message}` }],
          details: {},
        };
      },
    });
  });
}
```

## Key Points

1. **Register at `session_start`**: Tools registered in this event become available after the session is initialized
2. **Use `pi.registerTool()`**: The standard way to add custom tools
3. **Check availability**: Use `session.getAllTools()` to verify the tool is registered
4. **Active tools**: Use `session.getActiveToolNames()` to see which tools are currently active

## Testing

You can verify the dynamic tool is working by checking:

```typescript
// Before session_start
session.getAllTools().some((t) => t.name === "dynamic_tool") // false

// After session_start (via bindExtensions)
session.getAllTools().some((t) => t.name === "dynamic_tool") // true
```

## See Also

- [docs/extensions.md](../../docs/extensions.md) for full extension documentation
- [agent-session-dynamic-tools.test.ts](../../test/agent-session-dynamic-tools.test.ts) for test coverage

