{"body":"## Human explanation
What looks like an upstream? tool call failure when using Codex, leads to a broken session:

<img width="1023" height="760" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b32c3575-c4ba-4599-8254-e2170dcab18b" />

Repeatedly entering "continue" won't recover the session - it seems like the latest message corrupted things. 

`Error: No tool call found for function call output with call_id call_KXHLl4OkJLqXnzhwMKjeCdHX.`

## LLM-written analysis
### What I saw
- Session: `/Users/josh/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-josh-code-gohome--/2026-01-17T16-42-08-945Z_b0026b27-4539-4693-a14b-98eeedbca3fd.jsonl`
- Tool call for `call_KXHLl4OkJLqXnzhwMKjeCdHX` appears inside an assistant message that ends in `stopReason:"error"` with `errorMessage:"terminated"` (line 193 in the session file).
- Subsequent resume attempts (`continue`, `continue?`) produce OpenAI errors: `No tool call found for function call output with call_id call_KXHLl4OkJLqXnzhwMKjeCdHX` (lines 195, 197, 200).
- The call_id appears only 4 times total (tool call + 3 error messages); no tool_result entry exists in the session log.

### Why it fails
- `convertAssistantMessage()` skips tool calls if `stopReason === "error"` (`packages/ai/src/providers/openai-codex-responses.ts:350`).
- `convertToolResult()` always emits `function_call_output` (`packages/ai/src/providers/openai-codex-responses.ts:365`, `packages/ai/src/providers/openai-codex-responses.ts:377`).
- If a tool result is still emitted (from pending tool execution or replay) but the tool call is omitted from the converted history, the Codex request contains a `function_call_output` without a matching `function_call`. OpenAI rejects this with the error above.

### Expected
- Do not send `function_call_output` unless the corresponding `function_call` is included in the converted request context.

### Repro
1) Resume the session above.
2) Send `continue`.
3) Observe the OpenAI error about missing call_id.

### Notes
- This is an OpenAI validation error triggered by a pi-side message conversion/state mismatch; retries will repeatedly resend the same invalid request.
